    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d695">

                <pb facs="0963" n="861" sameAs="frus:frus1933v01/pg861"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 Estonia/124</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Estonian Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Seljamaa</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi><anchor n="61" xml:id="d695-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">12–R</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tallinn</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-11-16">November 16,
                        1933</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: By notes dated November 28,
                        1932,<anchor n="62" xml:id="d695-f2"/> December 15, 1932,<anchor n="63"
                        xml:id="d695-f3"/> and June 13, 1933, the Estonian Government had the honour
                    to inform the Government of the United States of America of the economic and
                    financial reasons on account of which it had not been in a position to effect
                    the payment of the installments due on December 15, 1932, and on June 15, 1933,
                    under the terms of the Debt Funding Agreement of 1925, and to request the
                    Government of the United States of America to agree to a friendly exchange of
                    views regarding the possibility of a reconsideration of the Debt Agreement of
                    1925.</p>
                <pb facs="0964" n="862" xml:id="pg862"/>
                <p>In view of the circumstance that the economic and financial conditions in Estonia
                    have up to now not shown any improvement, I have the honour to inform Your
                    Excellency that the Government of Estonia will unfortunately not be able to
                    effect the payment of the installment falling due on December 15, 1933.</p>
                <p>I avail myself [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jul. Seljamaa</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
